+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales`: accepts `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  `ticket` is a nonempty identifier, `soldAt` an ISO instant with timezone,
+  `dishId` an existing dish and `qty` a positive whole number of portions.
+  Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`: new distinct tickets and total
+  dish portions imported. All rows of previously imported tickets are skipped.
+  Validation includes skipped rows. A `sales_row` error names the failing row
+  (header is row 1); the entire file leaves stock, sales and ledger unchanged.
+  Consumption follows FEFO with `ref` `sale:<ticket>` and `at` set to `soldAt`.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`: returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 3, "actual": 4, "variance": 1 }`, sorted
+  by item id, including items with positive theoretical or actual use.
+  Days are inclusive UTC days; `from` must be on or before `to`.
+  Theoretical use sums ingredient snapshots of imported sales; actual use sums
+  every `consume` movement, including sales and cooking. Variance is actual
+  minus theoretical, in the item's unit, rounded to three decimal places.
